WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:04.020
A fairground stall,
one fair six-sided die.

2
00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:08.720
The sign: a pound a go,
roll a six, win five pounds!

3
00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:10.470
You pay a pound a go.

4
00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:13.210
Roll a six and you're handed five pounds,

5
00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:15.380
but your pound is not returned.

6
00:00:15.430 --> 00:00:17.940
A two, a six, a four.

7
00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:20.050
Coins wobble up and down.

8
00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:22.270
Five to one sounds generous.

9
00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:24.970
But over many games, is it fair?

10
00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:28.650
In this mission, you'll set up
a random variable for the gain,

11
00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:32.630
winnings minus the cost to
play, and its probabilities.

12
00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:36.690
You'll find the expected value:
the long-run average of X.

13
00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:40.770
And you'll see a game is fair
when the expected gain is zero.

14
00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:44.120
Your mission: decide whether
the dice game is fair.
